; RockCluster2 — one of 4 Rock terrain cluster variants (D-42 model_scenes variety pass).
; Composes 4 instances of the SAME newly-sourced small rock (Rock_2.glb, "Rock" by
; Quaternius, CC0, poly.pizza — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres) at varied position/
; rotation/scale jitter — same repetition-plus-variation idiom as
; GrassCommonShort.tscn's scattered cluster.
;
; Rock_2 raw measured AABB: footprint 0.155x0.147, height 0.190 tile-units — already a
; genuinely SMALL rock at natural scale (no giant-boulder problem here), so this variant
; needed only mild jitter (0.85x-1.25x) rather than a big scale-down, unlike
; RockCluster1's reused Rock_1 piece. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: density (4 rocks) and
; jitter amounts are first-pass judgment calls.
;
; Slab matches the existing Rock terrain grey (Color(0.55, 0.55, 0.58, 1)).
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap) — same fix,
; same reasoning as CommonTree1.tscn's header. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched.
